#######
# Setup
#######

Context('Numeric');
$v = random(45, 90, 1);
$t = NumberWithUnits(($v+sqrt($v**2 + 384))/32, 'seconds');

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
On Earth, if you throw a baseball straight up at speed [`v`] (in feet per second), it will land after [`\frac{v+\sqrt{v^2+384}}{32}`] seconds.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
If thrown straight up with speed [`[$v]`] feet per second, how long will it be until the baseball hits the ground?

[_]{$t}{10}

END_PGML

